* Read-only authorities for IyziTrace's IBM MQ metrics container, for one queue manager.
* Run on each queue manager as an MQ administrator:
*   runmqsc QMNAME < monitor-authorities.mqsc
* The operating-system group iyzmon, and a user in it, must exist on the queue manager's host first
* (docs/07-ibm-mq.md, step 1). Nothing here allows reading, writing or removing an application's
* messages: on application queues the group gets display and inquire only.
*
* Keep it read-only. The container also asks to reset queue statistics and reads the queue manager's
* event queues (SYSTEM.ADMIN.*.EVENT), which removes the events it reads. With these authorities
* the queue manager refuses both (reason 2035): no statistics are reset, no events are removed.

* Connect, and read the queue manager's attributes and status.
SET AUTHREC OBJTYPE(QMGR) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(CONNECT, INQ, DSP)

* Send DISPLAY commands to the command server (PCF) and receive the answers on a temporary queue
* made from the model queue.
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('SYSTEM.ADMIN.COMMAND.QUEUE') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(PUT, INQ, DSP)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('SYSTEM.DEFAULT.MODEL.QUEUE') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(GET, INQ, DSP)

* Status of every queue (depth, oldest message, time on queue) and every channel.
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('**') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(INQ, DSP)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('**') OBJTYPE(CHANNEL) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(DSP)
* Client-connection channels are a separate object type; without this, every channel inquiry logs
* AMQ8245W for them.
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('**') OBJTYPE(CLNTCONN) GROUP('iyzmon') AUTHADD(DSP)
